From: vllm-xpu-nix <noreply@anthropic.com>
Subject: [PATCH] fa2 xe2: stage umbrella header for attn_kernels_xe_2 PCH

The attn_kernels_xe_2 library generates ~3.6k TUs after the dtype split
(0007-fa2-dtype-split.patch). chunk_prefill.hpp and paged_decode.hpp
share almost their entire transitive header set (cute, the CUTLASS-SYCL
collective stack, sycl runtime, flash_attention_v2 fusion / scheduler /
epilogue, the FMHAKernel / PagedDecode kernel templates). The original
plan for this patch was to amortise that parse cost via a shared PCH:
`target_precompile_headers(attn_kernels_xe_2 PRIVATE attn_pch.hpp)`
with the umbrella header pulling both kernel-template surfaces in once
so cmake's auto-injected `-Xclang -include-pch` plumbing fans the
pre-parsed AST snapshot across every per-TU compile.

icpx 2025.3 blocks the PCH path outright:
  - the driver rejects -emit-pch under -fsycl ("precompiled header
    generation is not supported with '-fsycl'", visible at the driver
    level via -save-temps);
  - the default flow tries to bundle host+device PCH outputs through
    clang-offload-bundler with --type=pchi, which the bundler doesn't
    accept ("'pchi': invalid file type specified" — only i, ii, cui,
    hipi, d, ll, bc, s, o, gch, ast, a, ao, aoo are registered);
  - compiling the PCH without -fsycl works, but consumer -fsycl TUs
    reject it on the device pass: target 'x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu' vs
    'spir64_gen-unknown-unknown'. icpx 2025.3 has no flag that routes
    a per-pass -include-pch to skip PCH loading on the device pass
    (-Xsycl-target-frontend can't carry multi-token argument flags;
    -Xarch_device is CUDA-only and is filtered out before reaching the
    SYCL frontend).

Force-including the umbrella header textually via `target_compile_-
options(... -include attn_pch.hpp)` is also a regression on launcher
TUs (fmha_xe2.cpp pulls only chunk_prefill.hpp; paged_decode_xe2.cpp
pulls only paged_decode.hpp). Adding the other kernel-template surface
to both launchers doubles the in-frontend SYCL template work — the
paged_decode_xe2.cpp launcher peaks at ~77 GB RSS during the device
-cc1 pass (vs ~30-40 GB without the cross-include) and gets OOM-killed
on 96 GB hosts. The dtype split (0007) was specifically about reducing
per-TU peak RSS; re-bloating the launchers via a textual umbrella
defeats that.

This patch lands the umbrella file as a no-op sentinel for now. It
documents the PCH intent, captures the icpx 2025.3 blocker for future
reference, and gives `target_precompile_headers(...)` a single place to
point at once the toolchain ships SYCL+PCH support. CMakeLists.txt is
not touched: TUs continue to include only the kernel-template surface
they dispatch into, so the patch is a true no-op on build wall time
and per-TU peak RSS today.

When a post-2025.3 icpx fixes the bundler quirk, finishing this patch
is a two-line change: add the `#include "chunk_prefill.hpp"` /
`#include "paged_decode.hpp"` pair to attn_pch.hpp and add
`target_precompile_headers(attn_kernels_xe_2 PRIVATE attn_pch.hpp)` to
CMakeLists.txt. The SYCL kernel-name forward declarations in the
umbrella are pre-staged for that change — under `-fpch-instantiate-
templates` (which target_precompile_headers implicitly enables) icpx's
SYCL kernel-name validator runs the ETS tags in cute/util/compat/-
memory.hpp's `parallel_for<class memcpy_3d_detail>` against namespace-
scope visibility; without the pre-declarations the PCH-emit pass fails
with "kernel name should be forward declarable at namespace scope".

Expected effect once the PCH path lands: ~20-30% wall-time reduction
on FA2 kernel TUs, ~1-2 GB per-TU peak RSS drop (frontend parse cost
amortised once per cmake configure). Effect today: none.

diff --git a/csrc/xpu/attn/xe_2/attn_pch.hpp b/csrc/xpu/attn/xe_2/attn_pch.hpp
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..3a32d39
--- /dev/null
+++ b/csrc/xpu/attn/xe_2/attn_pch.hpp
@@ -0,0 +1,57 @@
+#pragma once
+
+// Umbrella header for the attn_kernels_xe_2 library — staged for a
+// future `target_precompile_headers(...)` adoption once icpx ships
+// SYCL+PCH support.
+//
+// chunk_prefill.hpp and paged_decode.hpp share almost their entire
+// transitive header set (cute, the CUTLASS-SYCL collective stack, sycl
+// runtime, flash_attention_v2 fusion / scheduler / epilogue, the
+// FMHAKernel / PagedDecode kernel templates). The dtype-split
+// (0007-fa2-dtype-split.patch) generates ~3.6k kernel TUs, each of
+// which pays that transitive parse cost independently. A shared PCH
+// would collapse that cost into one cmake configure.
+//
+// icpx 2025.3 blocks the PCH path:
+//   error: precompiled header generation is not supported with '-fsycl'
+// (visible at the driver level via `-save-temps`; the default flow
+// instead tries to bundle host+device PCH outputs through
+// clang-offload-bundler with `--type=pchi`, which the bundler doesn't
+// accept — only i, ii, cui, hipi, d, ll, bc, s, o, gch, ast, a, ao,
+// aoo are registered file types). Compiling the PCH without `-fsycl`
+// works but the consumer device pass rejects it on a target mismatch
+// (`x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu` vs `spir64_gen-unknown-unknown`); icpx
+// 2025.3 has no flag that routes a per-pass `-include-pch` to skip PCH
+// loading on the device pass.
+//
+// Until a post-2025.3 icpx ships SYCL+PCH support this header is a
+// no-op — it is intentionally NOT referenced from CMakeLists.txt. Both
+// kernel-template `#include`s below are commented out so a stray
+// `-include attn_pch.hpp` (or a partial cherry-pick) cannot bloat
+// launcher TUs by pulling in the other kernel-template surface.
+// Finishing the PCH adoption is a two-line change in this file plus
+// one line in CMakeLists.txt — uncomment the includes here, and add:
+//
+//   target_precompile_headers(attn_kernels_xe_2 PRIVATE attn_pch.hpp)
+
+// Pre-declare the SYCL kernel-name tags used inside
+// cute/util/compat/memory.hpp's `parallel_for<class T>` ETS forward
+// declarations. Under `-fpch-instantiate-templates` (which cmake's
+// target_precompile_headers implicitly enables) icpx eagerly
+// instantiates SYCL kernel templates during PCH-emit and the
+// kernel-name validator runs the ETS tags before the implicit
+// namespace-scope declaration has propagated, failing with "kernel
+// name should be forward declarable at namespace scope". Declaring the
+// tags here at namespace scope makes the in-body ETS a redeclaration
+// of an already-visible class, which the validator accepts. The
+// pre-declarations are also benign when this header is unreferenced
+// (today's state).
+namespace compat {
+namespace detail {
+class memcpy_3d_detail;
+class compat_memcpy_3d_detail_usmnone;
+} // namespace detail
+} // namespace compat
+
+// #include "chunk_prefill.hpp"
+// #include "paged_decode.hpp"
